heocr runs, when they are installed, these separate programs, which it does not bundle:
- Tesseract OCR (Apache License 2.0);
- LibreOffice (Mozilla Public License 2.0).

With the optional `tables` extra (pip install 'heocr[tables]'), heocr uses these separately installed components,
which it does not bundle:
- Docling and docling-ibm-models (MIT License);
- the docling-layout-heron layout model weights (Apache License 2.0);
- the TableFormer weights in docling-models (CDLA-Permissive-2.0 and Apache License 2.0).
The weights are fetched by the user at pinned revisions and checked by sha256 (see heocr.tableformer).
